2026-11-17 12:58:31 - Agent_20261117125514 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed 2 CodeQL queries with 4 total results. All findings were confirmed as true positives:

1. **Weak Random Number Generation (CWE-338)** at src/click/_compat.py:429 - Uses random.randrange() instead of secrets module for security-sensitive temporary filename generation in atomic file operations.

2. **TOCTOU Race Condition (CWE-367)** at src/click/_compat.py:438 - os.path.isdir() check on e.filename followed by os.access() without proper synchronization, allowing race condition between check and operation.

3. **TOCTOU Race Conditions (CWE-367)** at src/click/utils.py:559-560 - Two consecutive os.path.exists() checks (checking for path and path.exe) that can change state between checks and actual file operations, creating race conditions on Windows systems during module execution determination.

All vulnerabilities are legitimate security issues involving weak randomness and time-of-check-time-of-use (TOCTOU) race conditions in file operations.
